<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Read the MushroomScope privacy policy, including information about analytics, advertising, cookies, and your choices."><div class="shell py-8"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Privacy Policy'}]} /></div><article class="shell max-w-4xl py-12"><h1 class="font-serif text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: July 31, 2026</p><div class="prose mt-8"><p>MushroomScope is designed to collect as little personal information as practical. This policy explains the services that may operate when their configuration is enabled.</p><h2>Analytics and advertising</h2><p>We may use Google Analytics to understand aggregate site usage and Google AdSense to fund our work. Google and other advertising partners may place or read cookies, use web beacons, or process IP addresses and other identifiers to measure and serve advertising. Learn <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="external">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p><h2>Consent and choices</h2><p>Where required, visitors will be offered privacy choices before non-essential storage or personalized advertising is used. Browser controls can also block or delete cookies. Advertising choices may affect whether ads are personalized, but not necessarily whether ads appear.</p><h2>Contact messages</h2><p>If you email us, we receive the information you provide and use it to respond, maintain records, prevent abuse, and improve the site. We do not sell contact details.</p><h2>Data retention and rights</h2><p>Information is retained only as reasonably needed for the stated purpose, security, legal obligations, or dispute resolution. Depending on location, visitors may have rights to request access, correction, deletion, restriction, or objection.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions or privacy requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@mushroomscope.com">hello@mushroomscope.com</a>.</p></div></article></BaseLayout>
